<title>FRANCE: LVMH 1996 net attrib falls after charge.</title>
<headline>LVMH 1996 net attrib falls after charge.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   3,683  vs	   4,047</p>
<p>    Net excl exceptionals, goodwill</p>
<p>			     amortisation	4,457	up 6 percent</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		    20.40  vs	   19.25</p>
<p>    Exceptional			  charge  615  vs	    --</p>
<p>    Operating				    7,022  vs	   7,285</p>
<p>Operating by branch</p>
<p>	-- champagnes and wines		1,246  vs	   1,064</p>
<p>	-- cognacs and spirits		 1,560  vs	   1,678</p>
<p>	-- leather goods			 3,903  vs	   3,477</p>
<p>	-- perfumes/beauty products	    592  vs	   1,256</p>
<p>	-- other, incl expenses	 loss   279  vs     loss  190</p>
<p>    Turnover				    31,142  vs	  29,775</p>
<p>NOTE - LVMH gave its results in a statement. It said the 615 million charge for 1996 is due primarily to the impact of the sale of Guinness shares. The group sold a third of its Guinness stake last year.</p>
<p>LVMH said the fall in operating profit at its perfumes and beauty products division reflected the group's effort to increase selectivity in distribution to stem sales to parallel channels. It said the branch's product launches were successful.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman said the 1995 profit excluding exceptionals and goodwill amortisation was 4,196 million francs. The group had not published that figure last year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
